-- title:
--   Divisor expansions at level p² generate ℚ(j,jₚ,j_{p²})
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime. Inside the field $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ \mathbb{Q}$ of formal Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$ one has the element `jq`, namely $q^{-1}$ (the Hahn series `single (-1) 1`) times the image of the integral power series `jNum` under $\mathbb{Z}\to\mathbb{Q}$, i.e. the $q$-expansion of the $j$-invariant; and for each $N\neq 0$ the ring homomorphism `qExpand ℚ N`, which rescales exponents by multiplication by $N$ (substitution $q\mapsto q^{N}$), with `jqN N` its value at `jq`, i.e. $j(q^{N})$. The intermediate field `modularFunctionFieldFull N` is defined as the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ \mathbb{Q}$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the set `divisorExpansions N` of all `qExpand ℚ d jq` with $d$ a nonzero divisor of $N$. The theorem asserts the equality of intermediate fields
--   $$\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldFull}(p\cdot p)=\mathbb{Q}\bigl(\mathtt{jq},\ \mathtt{jqN}\ p,\ \mathtt{jqN}\ (p\cdot p)\bigr),$$
--   that is, the field generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the expansions attached to all divisors of $p^{2}$ coincides with the field generated by the three elements $j(q)$, $j(q^{p})$ and $j(q^{p^{2}})$.
--
--   This identifies the generators of the formal $q$-expansion model of the function field at level $p^{2}$, the divisors of $p^{2}$ being $1$, $p$ and $p^{2}$; it is a bookkeeping step in the purely algebraic determination of the degree of the modular equation at prime-square level. It is used by [`ModularCurve.exists_isFrickeAutFull_sq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_isFrickeAutFull_sq), [`ModularCurve.functionFieldGeneration_sq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.functionFieldGeneration_sq) and [`ModularCurve.relfinrank_full_sq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.relfinrank_full_sq).
